[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A\u001b[37m  The task is to devise a phased reverse-engineering plan for the Gamma mini synth, focusing on safety and lever...\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  A comprehensive, safety-first reverse-engineering plan has been designed and written to \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk2740b7d99226e250;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/PLAN.md\u0007PLAN.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\r\n\n  \u001b[1m### Summary of the Phased Reverse-Engineering Roadmap\u001b[m\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mSafety Interlocks & Anti-Contention Rules\u001b[m\n\u001b[40D• \u001b[1mHigh-Impedance Default:\u001b[m All unverified pins remain configured as \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk40776ce591ad8db5;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/per/gpio.h#L27\u0007GPIO::Mode::INPUT\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 or \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk86e766ec022b9612;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/per/gpio.h#L30\u0007GPIO::Mode::ANALOG\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\n\u001b[6Cto prevent shorts or damaged driver pads.\n\u001b[41D• \u001b[1mOpen-Drain Matrix Rule:\u001b[m Candidate key-matrix rows are strictly driven in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jke9d860e5609d31ad;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/per/gpio.h#L29\u0007GPIO::Mode"]
[0.000, "o", "::OPEN_DRAIN\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 with\r\n\u001b[6Cpull-up inputs to prevent V_{CC}–to–GND contention during simultaneous keypresses.\n\u001b[82D• \u001b[1mAcoustic Limiting:\u001b[m Test tone generation is clamped at -20 dBFS with \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkb97d61b17b14b9c4;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/DaisySP/Source/Utility/dsp.h#L115\u0007daisysp::SoftLimit\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and\n\u001b[92D\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8493a75e7d689000;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/DaisySP/Source/Utility/dcblock.h#L18\u0007daisysp::DcBlock\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mPhase 0: Non-Destructive Firmware Backup\u001b[m\n\u001b[39D• Boot into STM32 ROM DFU via \u001b[94mBOOT\u001b[m + \u001b[94mRESET\u001b[m.\n\u001b[43D• Check RDP protection level; dump Internal Flash (128 KB @ \u001b[94m0x080\u001b[5b\u001b[m) and QSPI Flash (8 MB @ \u001b[94m0x90\u001b[6b\u001b[m)\r\n\u001b[6Cvia \u001b[94mdfu-util\u001b[m.\n\u001b[13D• Archive SHA-256 hashes and analyze binary strings for peripheral identifiers.\r\n  3. \u001b[1mPhase 1: Safe Tooling & Non-Blocking USB CDC Shell\u001b[m\n\u001b[49D• Target Gamma's USB-C port routed to pins \u001b[94mD29\u001b[m/\u001b[94mD30\u001b[m (\u001b[94mUsbHandle::FS_EXTERNAL\u001b[m).\n\u001b[76D• Implement"]
[0.000, "o", " a microsecond-guarded non-blocking logger using \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8e5d818b149bb4ba;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/sys/system.h\u0007System::GetUs()\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 to eliminate the \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk92de9be3b19d8fd7;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/hid/logger.h#L192\u0007Logger\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\u001b[99Dsynchronous deadlock hazard.\r\n  4. \u001b[1mPhase 2: I2C Bus Scanning & Subsystem Detection\u001b[m\n\u001b[46D• Execute SCL bus-recovery clocking (9 pulses to clear hung SDA lines).\n\u001b[71D• Swee\r\n\n⣻  \u001b[90mLoading.\u001b[94m..\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /voice (or press f5) to record your prompt with your microphone.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m───────────────"]
