[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[27A  A comprehensive, safety-first reverse-engineering plan has been designed and written to \u001b]8;id=jk333b3f8798872c0;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/PLAN.md\u001b\\\u001b[4;34;4mP\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mL\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mA\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mN\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m.\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mm\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\n  \u001b[1m### Summary of the Phased Reverse-Engineering Roadmap\u001b[m\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mSafety Interlocks & Anti-Contention Rules\u001b[m\n\u001b[40D• \u001b[1mHigh-Impedance Default:\u001b[m All unverified pins remain configured as \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkabdb3621b02f22e5;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/per/gpio.h#L27\u0007GPIO::Mode::INPUT\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 or \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk4709302a94ad5a42;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/per/gpio.h#L30\u0007GPIO::Mode::ANALOG\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\n\u001b[6Cto prevent shorts or damaged driver pads.\n\u001b[41D• \u001b[1mOpen-Drain Matrix Rule:\u001b[m Candidate key-matrix rows are strictly driven in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk553caa217f1fa05d;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/per/gpio.h#L29\u0007GPIO::Mode::OPEN_DRAIN\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 with\r\n\u001b[6Cpull-up inputs to "]
[0.000, "o", "prevent V_{CC}–to–GND contention during simultaneous keypresses.\n\u001b[82D• \u001b[1mAcoustic Limiting:\u001b[m Test tone generation is clamped at -20 dBFS with \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk45125c94ff166414;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/DaisySP/Source/Utility/dsp.h#L115\u0007daisysp::SoftLimit\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and\n\u001b[92D\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk2af6b810b4f97d10;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/DaisySP/Source/Utility/dcblock.h#L18\u0007daisysp::DcBlock\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mPhase 0: Non-Destructive Firmware Backup\u001b[m\n\u001b[39D• Boot into STM32 ROM DFU via \u001b[94mBOOT\u001b[m + \u001b[94mRESET\u001b[m.\n\u001b[43D• Check RDP protection level; dump Internal Flash (128 KB @ \u001b[94m0x080\u001b[5b\u001b[m) and QSPI Flash (8 MB @ \u001b[94m0x90\u001b[6b\u001b[m)\r\n\u001b[6Cvia \u001b[94mdfu-util\u001b[m.\n\u001b[13D• Archive SHA-256 hashes and analyze binary strings for peripheral identifiers.\r\n  3. \u001b[1mPhase 1: Safe Tooling & Non-Blocking USB CDC Shell\u001b[m\n\u001b[49D• Target Gamma's USB-C port routed to pins \u001b[94mD29\u001b[m/\u001b[94mD30\u001b[m (\u001b[94mUsbHandle::FS_EXTERNAL\u001b[m).\n\u001b[76D• Implement a microsecond-guarded non-blocking logger using \u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkc5da88efd6829dea;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/sys/system.h\u0007System::GetUs()\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 to eliminate the \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk9f9119fb7c4d2b87;file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/hid/logger.h#L192\u0007Logger\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\u001b[99Dsynchronous deadlock hazard.\r\n  4. \u001b[1mPhase 2: I2C Bus Scanning & Subsystem Detection\u001b[m\n\u001b[46D• Execute SCL bus-recovery clocking (9 pulses to clear hung SDA lines).\n\u001b[71D• Sweep 7-bit addresses (\u001b[94m0x08\u001b[m to \u001b[94m0x77\u001b[m) using\n\u001b[44D[\u001b[94mI2CHandle\u001b[m](file:///Users/brett/tmp/workspace/libDaisy/src/per/i2c.\r\n\n⣾  \u001b[90mLoading...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /voice (or press f5) to record your prompt with your microphone.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
